{"name":"Cyclamen","hex":"#d687ba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cyclamen","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Primulaceae – cyclamens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cyclamen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cyclamen","blocks":[{"text":"Cyclamen is a genus of 25 species of perennial flowering plants in the family Primulaceae. In English, it is known by the common name sowbread, or, by the genus name as cyclamen. The species are native to Europe and the Mediterranean Basin east to the Caucasus and Iran, with one species in Somalia. They grow from tubers and are valued for their flowers with upswept petals and variably patterned leaves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Cyclamen_purpurascens_sl3.jpg/330px-Cyclamen_purpurascens_sl3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclamen"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/RakefetMetzuya.jpg/500px-RakefetMetzuya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/RakefetMetzuya.jpg/1280px-RakefetMetzuya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/RakefetMetzuya.jpg/500px-RakefetMetzuya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARakefetMetzuya.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Cyclamen_root_shape_en_1.jpg/500px-Cyclamen_root_shape_en_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Cyclamen_root_shape_en_1.jpg/1280px-Cyclamen_root_shape_en_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content